<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	The one launchd job this product registers (ADR-001 D3): a user LaunchAgent that runs the
	Supervisor, which in turn owns the three FrankenPHP children. Installed by the app build at
	Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/ and registered with SMAppService.agent(plistName:) from the
	installer's BOOT_SERVICES state. The file name, the Label and the bundle-id prefix are the
	A12 placeholder `se.stafe.executive-ai` (apps/macos/Config/Shared.xcconfig LXAI_BUNDLE_PREFIX).

	BundleProgram points inside the Supervisor's own helper application bundle
	(Contents/Helpers/LaravelExecutiveAISupervisor.app) rather than at a bare tool in
	Contents/MacOS/, because `keychain-access-groups` is a restricted entitlement that macOS
	validates at launch against an embedded provisioning profile and only a bundle can carry one
	(A24, decided 2026-10-11 on the evidence of the first signed build; ADR-003 D5, ADR-001 D3 as
	amended).

	Nothing here is per machine: no absolute path, no user name, no port and no secret. The
	Supervisor derives every path from its own bundle and the user's Library at run time, and
	secrets never travel through launchd (ADR-003 D7 row 12).

	Semantics under SMAppService (man 5 launchd.plist, ADR-001 V2):
	  BundleProgram    app-bundle-relative executable; only valid for SMAppService-installed plists.
	                   Here: the inner executable of the embedded helper bundle.
	  RunAtLoad        start as soon as the agent is bootstrapped (register() and every login)
	  KeepAlive        relaunch whenever the Supervisor exits, for any reason; launchd throttles
	                   a job that exits faster than ThrottleInterval
	  ThrottleInterval the outer restart guarantee — at most one Supervisor launch per 10 s;
	                   the bounded, health-driven inner restarts live in the Supervisor itself
	  ProcessType      Background: resource limits that keep it from disrupting the user
	  ExitTimeOut      seconds launchd waits after SIGTERM before SIGKILL; the Supervisor uses
	                   that window to stop its children cleanly
	  MachServices     the XPC control service the GUI connects to (ipc-contract §7); launchd
	                   checks it in so NSXPCListener(machServiceName:) can serve it
	  LimitLoadToSessionType  Aqua: a user GUI session, which is what a LaunchAgent is for
	  AssociatedBundleIdentifiers  which bundles System Settings → Login Items attributes this job
	                   to (man 5 launchd.plist): the app the user recognises, and the helper bundle
	                   that is actually launched, so the entry is attributed to this product either
	                   way
	-->
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>se.stafe.executive-ai.supervisor</string>
	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/Helpers/LaravelExecutiveAISupervisor.app/Contents/MacOS/LaravelExecutiveAISupervisor</string>
	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>se.stafe.executive-ai.app</string>
		<string>se.stafe.executive-ai.supervisor</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>10</integer>
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Background</string>
	<key>ExitTimeOut</key>
	<integer>30</integer>
	<key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
	<string>Aqua</string>
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>se.stafe.executive-ai.supervisor.control</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
